  "slug": "minimum-size-subarray-sum",
  "title": "Minimum Size Subarray Sum",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Sliding window",
  "patterns": [
    "sliding window",
    "variable-size window"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "since all numbers are positive, what happens to the window's sum as you shrink it from the left? does it only ever move in one direction?",
    "grow the window by moving the right edge forward, adding to a running sum, until the sum is at least the target",
    "once the target is met, that's a valid window - can you shrink it from the left while it's still valid, to find something shorter?",
    "keep shrinking from the left (subtracting from the running sum and updating the best length) until the sum drops below target, then go back to growing the right edge"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "forgetting to update the minimum length while shrinking, only checking it when first reaching the target",
    "not shrinking as far as possible before growing again, missing shorter valid windows",
    "returning the window size when no valid window was ever found, instead of 0"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a list of positive integers `nums` and a target sum.\n\n**Find the length of the shortest contiguous subarray whose sum is greater than or equal to the target. If no such subarray exists, return 0.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= target <= 10^9",
      "1 <= nums.length <= 10^5",
      "1 <= nums[i] <= 10^4"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "the whole array is needed to reach the target",
      "a single element already meets or exceeds the target",
      "the target is larger than the sum of the entire array"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
